# Nissan Bluebird T72 four-door saloon, 1986-1990.
#
# The T72 is the same Auster-based shell as the T12, but built at Washington,
# Tyne and Wear from July 1986 instead of imported from Japan. The facelifted
# 1989-90 car is modelled, with the split grille; the early T72 nose and the
# hatchback added in January 1987 are not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Violet
#
# Dimensions 4.400 x 1.690 x 1.395 m, wheelbase 2.550 m — identical to the T12
# because it is the same body. The shell was inherited from the T12 master
# rather than rebuilt. Side indicators take the modelled width to 1.702 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the T72 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: silver, blue, red and white, the same four as the T12. Weights
# silver 3, blue 3, red 2, white 2, total 10, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h for the 1.8. Comfort 82/453, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 82, a
# hair above the imported T12's 80/450 because the British-built car was better
# trimmed. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: July 1986 intro, retires staggered 2002-2005 on a
# fifteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-bluebird-t72.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-bluebird-t72.dae (52 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-bluebird-t72/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitation: no rear photograph of a facelift T72 saloon was available
# — the only rear view in the pack is of the hatchback, whose tail cannot verify
# a saloon. The revised rear-lamp subdivision is therefore provisional. At 128 px
# the notchback roofline and the split-grille nose read as the T72.

obj=citycar
